# Example --patterns file for hlse_core (roadmap P0-3 / P1-6).
#
# Use this to teach HLSE your organization's internal token formats AND
# protect your own name/executives from email impersonation — both without
# a rebuild:
#
#   hlse_core --patterns custom-patterns.example secret --stdin
#   hlse_core --patterns custom-patterns.example scan .
#   hlse_core --patterns custom-patterns.example email "<headers>"
#
# Format: one directive per line. '#' comments and blank lines are ignored.
#
# ── SECRET: custom credential patterns ──────────────────────────────────
#   SECRET <prefix> <min_suffix> <charset> <score> <label...>
#
#   prefix      literal token prefix to search for (e.g. "ACME_KEY_")
#   min_suffix  minimum number of <charset>-valid characters required
#               immediately after the prefix
#   charset     one of: alnum | alnum_dash | hex | alpha | digit
#   score       0-100 risk score for this credential type
#   label       free text (may contain spaces) — the credential type name
#               shown in findings; runs to end of line
#
# Checked with the exact same matching and placeholder/example-value
# suppression logic as HLSE's built-in secret-pattern table.
#
# ── BRAND: custom impersonation targets ──────────────────────────────────
#   BRAND <name> <owned_domain1>[,<owned_domain2>...]
#
#   name           matched as a whole word (case-insensitive) against the
#                  From display name of a scanned email
#   owned_domain*  comma-separated list (up to 4) of domains that
#                  legitimately send as this brand; no spaces
#
# If <name> appears in a From display name but the sending domain is not
# one of the registered owned domains, it fires the same E1 "display-name
# vs. From-domain mismatch" check that already protects major consumer
# brands (Microsoft, PayPal, ...) — e.g. "Acme Corp Finance" emailing from
# an attacker's domain instead of acmecorp.com.
#
# A malformed line (either directive) is skipped with a warning; the rest
# of the file still loads. Neither directive affects --benchmark (F1 is
# computed without --patterns).

# ACME Corp internal API key: "ACME_KEY_" + 20+ alphanumeric chars
SECRET ACME_KEY_ 20 alnum 85 ACME Internal API Key

# ACME Corp internal service token: "acme-svc-" + 16+ hex chars
SECRET acme-svc- 16 hex 70 ACME Service Token

# ACME Corp legacy deploy token: "DEPLOY-" + 24+ chars (letters/digits/-/_)
SECRET DEPLOY- 24 alnum_dash 75 ACME Legacy Deploy Token

# Protect "ACME Corp" impersonation in BEC/CEO-fraud emails: only
# acmecorp.com and acme-corp.com may legitimately claim this name
BRAND acmecorp acmecorp.com,acme-corp.com
